# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — contributor & executor contract

## Always

- Code, comments, error messages, commit messages, and any file inside
  this repo: **English**. Chat with the human: whatever language they're
  using.
- Run `{{TEST_COMMAND}}` before your first change in a session and after
  every logical unit. Never leave the suite red at a commit boundary.
- Atomic commits, one concern each, conventional-commit messages:
  `{{COMMIT_TYPES}}`.
- Never hand-edit generated or state files — use the project's own
  commands/scripts for anything that has one.
- No new dependencies without explicit human approval.

## Plan mode

If a `PLAN-*.md` file exists at the repo root, you are executing a planned
cycle. This changes the rules:

- Work on exactly ONE phase per session — the phase the human names. Never
  start the next phase, even if it looks trivial from here.
- The plan is the spec. If something in it is ambiguous or you believe it
  is wrong: **STOP and ask.** Deviating silently from the plan is the
  failure mode this whole contract exists to prevent — do not embody it.
- Findings referenced in the plan (a bug, a bypass, a failing case) become
  a failing test *before* the fix. Show the RED run, then fix, then GREEN.
- At phase end: tick (`- [x]`) only the acceptance criteria you can
  demonstrate right now — leave anything only a human can verify unticked
  and say so. Then report: files changed, tests added (and what each one
  guards against), any deviation from the plan with justification, and
  open questions. Then stop — the human audits the diff before merge.

## Definition of done for any phase

- All acceptance criteria in the plan for this phase: met and demonstrated,
  not asserted.
- Adversarial tests for every fix in the phase: present and green.
- The full existing test suite: green.
- No scope creep — anything tempting-but-tangential goes in the plan's
  "out of scope" section for a future cycle, not into this diff.
